<p>Apple’s overhaul of Siri and its expansion of Apple Intelligence are extensive. Take Control publisher Joe Kissell and I looked at this mountain of changes and opted to research and write an entirely new book, <em><a href="https://www.takecontrolbooks.com/siri-ai?PT=6COLORS">Take Control of Siri AI and Apple Intelligence</a></em>, to help us get a handle on what’s new and thus pass it along to readers. This title is now available in its 1.0 release, ahead of the version 27 operating systems shipping in September. We also have our books on <a href="https://www.takecontrolbooks.com/ios-27-ipados-27/?PT=6COLORS">iOS 27/iPadOS 27</a> and <a href="https://www.takecontrolbooks.com/golden-gate/?PT=6COLORS">Golden Gate</a> available in 1.0 versions. All will receive free updates when the production versions ship.</p>
<p>We look at everything related to Siri AI, including the new Siri app and its ability to handle contextually aware conversations, the expansion of Apple Intelligence into new apps, enhancements to accessibility features, and, in particular, Visual Intelligence’s heightened prominence as a camera feature on the iPhone and iPad. We also dive into how Apple’s Private Compute Cloud works and associated privacy issues, particularly around the company’s extension of this on-device processing to Apple-managed hardware at Google Cloud.</p>
